Stage 27 — Common Enterprise Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Treating enterprise applications like small Android apps.

Reading classes alphabetically instead of following business domains.

Confusing infrastructure code with business rules.

Ignoring dependency injection and module boundaries.

Overlooking background synchronization and offline workflows.

Focusing on UI implementation before reconstructing business processes.



---

Stage 28 — Enterprise APK Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify and profile large-scale enterprise Android applications.

✅ Recover business domains, modular architecture, and dependency graphs.

✅ Reconstruct workflows, repositories, persistence, networking, synchronization, and state management.

✅ Understand the structural role of authentication, authorization, configuration, and external integrations.

✅ Distinguish infrastructure from business logic and map cross-domain dependencies.

✅ Validate architectural understanding through runtime observations.

✅ Produce comprehensive documentation describing the application's business capabilities, architecture, execution model, and subsystem interactions.



